.\" fgetc.3 - character input/output on streams
.TH FGETC 3 "May 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
fgetc, getc, getchar, fputc, putc, putchar, ungetc \- character input/output on streams
.SH LIBRARY
.B libc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fgetc(FILE *" stream ");"
.PP
.BI "int getc(FILE *" stream ");"
.PP
.B "int getchar(void);"
.PP
.BI "int fputc(int " c ", FILE *" stream ");"
.PP
.BI "int putc(int " c ", FILE *" stream ");"
.PP
.BI "int putchar(int " c ");"
.PP
.BI "int ungetc(int " c ", FILE *" stream ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fgetc ()
reads the next character from
.I stream
and returns it as an
.I unsigned char
cast to an
.IR int ,
or
.B EOF
on end of file or error.
.PP
.BR getc ()
is equivalent to
.BR fgetc ().
In Substrate's libc it is implemented as a function (not a macro), so
.I stream
is evaluated only once.
.PP
.BR getchar ()
is equivalent to
.BI fgetc( stdin ).
.PP
.BR fputc ()
writes the character
.IR c ,
cast to an
.IR "unsigned char" ,
to
.IR stream .
.PP
.BR putc ()
is equivalent to
.BR fputc ().
As with
.BR getc (),
it is implemented as a function in Substrate's libc.
.PP
.BR putchar ( c )
is equivalent to
.BI fputc( c ", " stdout ).
.PP
.BR ungetc ()
pushes
.I c
back onto
.I stream
so that it will be returned by the next read operation on that stream.
The pushed-back character is converted to
.I unsigned char
and a successful call clears the end-of-file indicator for the stream.
.PP
Substrate's libc supports a single character of pushback per stream.
A second consecutive call to
.BR ungetc ()
without an intervening read will fail.
A successful call to
.BR fseek (3),
.BR fsetpos (3),
or
.BR rewind (3)
discards any pushed-back character.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR fgetc (),
.BR getc (),
and
.BR getchar ()
return the character read as an
.I unsigned char
cast to an
.IR int ,
or
.B EOF
on end of file or read error.
.PP
.BR fputc (),
.BR putc (),
and
.BR putchar ()
return the character written as an
.I unsigned char
cast to an
.IR int ,
or
.B EOF
on write error.
.PP
.BR ungetc ()
returns
.I c
on success, or
.B EOF
if
.I c
equals
.B EOF
or if a previous pushed-back character has not yet been consumed.
.BR ungetc ()
does not set the stream error indicator on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3),
.BR fread (3),
.BR fwrite (3),
.BR fgets (3),
.BR fputs (3),
.BR scanf (3),
.BR printf (3),
.BR feof (3),
.BR ferror (3)
.SH STANDARDS
.BR fgetc (),
.BR getc (),
.BR getchar (),
.BR fputc (),
.BR putc (),
.BR putchar (),
and
.BR ungetc ()
conform to ISO C90 and POSIX.1-2008.
The single-character pushback guarantee for
.BR ungetc ()
matches the minimum required by the standards; portable code should not assume more.
